Motorcycle Wheelie Controller tests
===================================

The Unity suite in `test_controller_core` covers the hardware-independent
controller state machine and persistent-settings validation.

Run the complete hardware-independent suite on this computer (no board):

    pio test -e native

Compile the on-device version without touching a connected board:

    pio test -e seeed_xiao_esp32s3 --without-uploading --without-testing

Run the tests on a connected XIAO ESP32-S3:

    pio test -e seeed_xiao_esp32s3

The on-device command temporarily uploads the test firmware. Upload the normal
application again afterward with:

    pio run -e seeed_xiao_esp32s3 --target upload

The native tests exercise the same portable helpers used by the firmware modules for
wheelie transitions, adaptive angle processing, warning hysteresis, light
patterns, fades, settings validation, and rollover-safe timing.
